\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces  State preparation error as a function of the number of state preparation pulses, $N$. The error is defined as population not in the $\mathinner {|{\downarrow }\rangle }$ state after the preparation sequence has been applied. The error is reduced to below $10^{-3}$ after $N=7$ pulses, which is used in our experiments. }}{49}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:stateprep}{{4.3}{49}{State preparation error as a function of the number of state preparation pulses, $N$. The error is defined as population not in the $\ket {\downarrow }$ state after the preparation sequence has been applied. The error is reduced to below $10^{-3}$ after $N=7$ pulses, which is used in our experiments}{figure.caption.16}{}}
